Please describe the bug 🐞
NamedReference::bind works by creating a Schema from the StructType parameter. This usually means repeated creation of the Schema instance, which involves re-computing fields like idToName, idToAccessor, etc. So I wonder whether we can have an interface to directly work with a Schema parameter?
The following code takes about 1400ms on my laptop. If I bind against the Schema instance, run time is reduced to 40ms.
public void test() throws Exception {
    List<Types.NestedField> fields = Lists.newArrayList();
    for (int i = 1; i <= 100; i++) {
      fields.add(Types.NestedField.optional(i, String.format("x%d", i), Types.IntegerType.get()));
    }
    Schema schema = new Schema(fields);
    Expression filter = Expressions.alwaysTrue();
    for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
      filter = Expressions.and(filter, Expressions.equal(String.format("x%d", i), i));
    }
    long start = System.currentTimeMillis();
    for (int i = 0; i < 10000; i++) {
      Binder.bind(schema.asStruct(), filter, false);
    }
    System.out.println(System.currentTimeMillis() - start);
  }
Some background: we implemented indexes that can be used to skip splits on Trino workers. For these indexes to work, the coordinator needs to distribute the filter expressions to workers. Therefore we need to access FileScanTask::residual on coordinator during split generation, which involves the evaluation and binding stuff. And we noticed it can become a hot spot method, or even the bottleneck of the whole query.

